From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sm8250: suspend the card and its streams

The card sets no PM ops, and qcom_snd_parse_of() marks every DPCM link
ignore_suspend, so snd_soc_suspend() never runs for it and open PCMs are
never suspended. Since the LPASS macros and SoundWire controllers are
force-suspended across system sleep, a stream left open at suspend kept
running into a clock-stopped bus, and the speakers stayed silent after
resume. Wire up snd_soc_pm_ops and clear ignore_suspend on this card's
links, as on sc8280xp; none of them has to run while the system sleeps.
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
index d81aed59e9cd..fad67b382d7e 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
@@ -163,6 +163,9 @@ static void sm8250_add_be_ops(struct snd_soc_card *card)
 			link->be_hw_params_fixup = sm8250_be_hw_params_fixup;
 			link->ops = &sm8250_be_ops;
 		}
+
+		/* Nothing on these cards has to play across system suspend */
+		link->ignore_suspend = 0;
 	}
 }
 
@@ -212,6 +215,7 @@ static struct platform_driver snd_sm8250_driver = {
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "snd-sm8250",
 		.of_match_table = snd_sm8250_dt_match,
+		.pm = &snd_soc_pm_ops,
 	},
 };
 module_platform_driver(snd_sm8250_driver);
